{"id":"ed63fb643e989ab7a11f2fede43d9f2d90eaafcc","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/d41586-026-02735-7","title":"When AI does science, who is accountable for mistakes?","site_name":"Buzzing","source":"www.nature.com","byline":"Chakraborty, Chiranjib","excerpt":"Letter to the Editor","content_html":"<DIV class=\"page\" id=\"readability-page-1\"><div id=\"content\" data-container-type=\"article\" data-component=\"article-container\">\n            \n\n            \n\n            <article data-track-component=\"news\" lang=\"en\">\n                \n                <div>\n                    \n                        <div>\n    <header>\n        <div>\n            <ul data-test=\"article-identifier\">\n                \n                    <li data-test=\"article-category\"><span>CORRESPONDENCE</span></li>\n                    <li>\n                        <time datetime=\"2026-09-01\">01 September 2026</time>\n                    </li>\n                \n                \n            </ul>\n\n            \n\n            \n        </div>\n        \n            <div>\n                \n                    <p><span>By</span></p><ul data-test=\"authors-list\" data-component-authors-activator=\"authors-list\">\n    \n        \n        <li>\n            <a data-test=\"author-name\" data-track=\"click\" data-track-label=\"view author info\" data-track-index=\"1_1\" data-track-context=\"researcher popup with no profile\" href=\"#author-0\" data-author-popup=\"author-0\" data-corresp-id=\"c0\">\n                Chiranjib Chakraborty</a><sup><a href=\"#Aff0\">0</a></sup></li>\n    \n</ul>\n\n\n<div data-test=\"author-info\">\n    <ol>\n        \n            <li>\n                \n                    <span><a id=\"corresp-c0\" href=\"mailto:drchiranjib@yahoo.com\" rel=\"nofollow\">Chiranjib Chakraborty</a></span>\n                \n                \n                    <ol>\n                        <li id=\"Aff0\">\n                            <p>Adamas University, Kolkata, India.</p>\n                        </li>\n                    </ol>\n                \n                \n                    \n                \n            </li>\n        \n    </ol>\n</div>\n\n                \n            </div>\n        \n    </header>\n\n    \n    \n    \n        \n            \n    \n\n        \n    \n</div>\n                    \n\n                    \n\n                    \n                        \n                        <p>Chris Lu and his colleagues describe an AI scientist that can generate hypotheses, conduct computational experiments, interpret results, write papers, and review its own work (<a href=\"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41586-026-10265-5\" data-track=\"click\" data-label=\"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41586-026-10265-5\" data-track-category=\"body text link\">C. Lu <i>et al</i>. <i>Nature </i><b>651</b>, 914–919; 2026</a>). As artificial-intelligence systems become more independent, responsibility for scientific outcomes could be divided up between users, institutions and developers.</p>\n                        \n                        \n                    \n                        <p><em>Nature</em> <strong>657</strong>, 312 (2026)</p>\n                        <p><em>doi: https://doi.org/10.1038/d41586-026-02735-7</em></p>\n\n                    \n                    <div id=\"competing-interests\" data-toggle=\"anchor-links-section\" data-label=\"Competing Interests\">\n                            <h2>Competing Interests</h2>\n                            <p>The author declares no competing interests.</p>\n                        </div>\n\n                    \n                        <h2 id=\"related-articles\">Related Articles</h2>\n                        <ul>\n    \n        <li>\n            <p>\n                <a href=\"https://www.nature.com/articles/d41586-026-01551-3\" data-track=\"click\" data-track-label=\"related article (rank:0)\">\n                    \n                        <img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"//media.nature.com/lw100/magazine-assets/d41586-026-02735-7/d41586-026-02735-7_52851272.jpg\" alt=\"\">\n                    \n                    Why AI cannot do good science without humans\n                </a>\n            </p>\n        </li>\n    \n        <li>\n            <p>\n                <a href=\"https://www.nature.com/articles/d41586-026-01954-2\" data-track=\"click\" data-track-label=\"related article (rank:1)\">\n                    \n                        <img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"//media.nature.com/lw100/magazine-assets/d41586-026-02735-7/d41586-026-02735-7_53002624.jpg\" alt=\"\">\n                    \n                    Will AI spark a scientific renaissance — or a diffuse monoculture?\n                </a>\n            </p>\n        </li>\n    \n        <li>\n            <p>\n                <a href=\"https://www.nature.com/articles/d41586-026-01557-x\" data-track=\"click\" data-track-label=\"related article (rank:2)\">\n                    \n                        <img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"//media.nature.com/lw100/magazine-assets/d41586-026-02735-7/d41586-026-02735-7_52722758.jpg\" alt=\"\">\n                    \n                    The uncritical adoption of AI in science is alarming — we urgently need guard rails\n                </a>\n            </p>\n        </li>\n    \n        <li>\n            <p>\n                <a href=\"https://www.nature.com/nature/articles?type=correspondence\" data-track=\"click\" data-track-label=\"related article (rank:3)\">\n                    \n                    See more letters to the editor\n                </a>\n            </p>\n        </li>\n    \n</ul>\n                    \n\n                    \n                        <h2 id=\"subjects\">Subjects</h2>\n                        \n                    <section data-component-tab-list=\"true\" data-track=\"in-view\" data-track-action=\"in-view\" data-track-category=\"latest content\" data-track-label=\"visible\">\n    <h2 id=\"tabl